# The build context is the repository root, because the API image needs both
# api/ and seed/. Everything below would otherwise be shipped to the daemon.

**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache

.git
.gitignore

# Local state. The containers use a volume; copying a laptop's database into
# an image would ship whatever was in it.
storage/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.log

# Secrets never enter a build context, at any depth -- web/.env.local would
# otherwise be copied into the image by `COPY web/ ./` and baked into a layer.
# The design key reaches the build as a mounted secret; the API key is
# runtime-only. `.env.example` is documentation and stays.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.design-key

# Screenshots, docs and the checks -- none of it runs in a container.
web/shots/
web/scripts/shots.mjs
docs/
*.md
!README.md

**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
